# Title: Suspicious LNK Double Extension File Created
# ID: 3215aa19-f060-4332-86d5-5602511f3ca8
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
# Date: 2022-11-07
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.007
# Description: Detects the creation of files with an "LNK" as a second extension. This is sometimes used by malware as a method to abuse the fact that Windows hides the "LNK" extension by default.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((file.path:*.lnk AND (file.path:*.doc.* OR file.path:*.docx.* OR file.path:*.jpg.* OR file.path:*.pdf.* OR file.path:*.ppt.* OR file.path:*.pptx.* OR file.path:*.xls.* OR file.path:*.xlsx.*)) AND NOT ((file.path:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Recent\\*)) AND NOT (((process.executable:*\\excel.exe AND file.path:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Excel*) OR (process.executable:*\\powerpnt.exe AND file.path:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\PowerPoint*) OR ((process.executable:*\\excel.exe OR process.executable:*\\powerpnt.exe OR process.executable:*\\winword.exe) AND file.path:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Office\\Recent\\*) OR (process.executable:*\\winword.exe AND file.path:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Word*))))
